          "heading": "The central engineering problem",
          "content": "## The central engineering problem\n\nSurvey work starts with a defined measurand: a coordinate, elevation, angle, distance or shape estimated under a stated frame, epoch, unit, and uncertainty. Coordinates without a reference system are only numbers.\n\nDistinguish repeatability from accuracy, random variation from instrument bias, ground distances from grid distances, and engineering-local frames from national geodetic frames.\n\nMake a chain of evidence from source observation through calibration, correction, reduction, adjustment and quality acceptance. A tidy map is not a substitute for independent checks."
