          "heading": "The central engineering problem",
          "content": "## The central engineering problem\n\nSlope distance is not horizontal distance. Prism constants, atmospheric refraction, instrument centering and alignment can produce systematic error even when repeats look consistent.\n\nAngular observations have circle-reading, pointing, collimation and centering errors; a complete series of faces and repeated sets can expose some instrument biases.\n\nCalibrations and field check shots must match intended tolerances. Corrections and uncertainty matter most where a small position error becomes a large construction or legal consequence."
