          "content": "## The central engineering problem\n\nA leveling circuit is a chain of backsight and foresight readings referenced to stable marks. The algebraic sum of height differences should match an independently established benchmark difference within project tolerance.\n\nGNSS ellipsoid heights and leveling orthometric heights are not interchangeable. Conversion using a specified geoid model is an approximation whose uncertainty must be recorded.\n\nClosure adjustment distributes the observed discrepancy according to the measurement design, but it does not repair a wrong benchmark, a changed instrument height or unstable turning points."
