          "secNumber": "4.1",
          "heading": "The central engineering problem",
          "content": "## The central engineering problem\n\nTraverse coordinates accumulate from lengths and directions. A closed polygon provides two independent closure components, and angular closure is an additional check.\n\nBowditch corrections are a practical length-proportional approximation under specified observation characteristics; rigorous least squares is preferable for heterogeneous and high-order control.\n\nControl networks should resist gross errors through redundancy, geometric strength and independently occupied checks; a mathematically small residual does not guarantee a correct datum."
