          "content": "## The central engineering problem\n\nGNSS positioning estimates receiver position and clock state from satellite measurements. Multipath, obstruction, ionosphere, troposphere and satellite geometry all affect results.\n\nDOP is a geometry amplification factor, not an absolute accuracy guarantee. A precise-looking number of decimal places does not establish coordinate quality.\n\nRTK and network correction techniques can be valuable but require ambiguity validation, initialization checks, reference-frame alignment and independent control observations."
