          "content": "## The central engineering problem\n\nDigital photogrammetry extracts geometric information from overlapping images tied to control; scale and elevation errors are sensitive to camera calibration and network geometry.\n\nLidar point density is not the same as verified vertical accuracy. Data processing, classification, independent checkpoints and a documented uncertainty report are needed for terrain products.\n\nGIS operations may silently change units, projections and spatial resolution. Metadata should preserve original frames, transformations, sources and dates."
