          "content": "## The central engineering problem\n\nEngineering setting-out transforms design coordinates into physically observable marks, offsets and checks. Wrong design versions and datum confusion can overwhelm excellent instrument precision.\n\nA deformation series requires repeated measurements to stable reference points and explicit assessment of reference motion, correlation, temperature and instrument drift.\n\nRoute surveys combine alignment geometry with topography, utilities and drainage constraints; small chainage errors can move an intervention to the wrong asset."
