          "content": "## Unit synthesis and reflection\n\nThe four lessons in survey deliverables connect observation, reduction, uncertainty, and decision. To demonstrate mastery, identify the single weakest piece of evidence in your worked case and propose a new observation that could change the recommendation. Report a sensitivity estimate, a separate independent validation check and an ethical or project safety constraint. End with a statement of what you would refuse to certify based on the available data.\n\nFor a fully documented result, preserve a table of raw values, correction quantities, accepted values, units and date. Use a table rather than only prose when comparing field sessions; in the accompanying experiment, try an extreme but physically meaningful input and explain the model breakdown."
